{
  "_comment": "Routing overlay merged with skill/agent frontmatter by scripts/build-routes.js into commander/cowork-plugin/hooks/lib/ccc-routes.json. strong = distinctive whole-word phrases (+0.6, enough for a menu alone); triggers = supporting phrases (+0.35 multi-word, +0.25 single word, never enough alone); patterns = request-shaped intent regex (+0.6, case-insensitive; topic mentions belong in strong/triggers); negatives = regex that removes the route; paths = file names/extensions mentioned in the prompt (+0.2); requirePath = score only when a path matches; next = the 'what next' graph read by the Stop handler; priority = integer tiebreak when two routes score the same (higher first, default 0); exclude = never route. A route with no signal at all fails the build. A menu needs 0.55; auto-run needs an intent pattern hit plus 0.8 with a 0.25 lead. Edit this file, run `npm run build:routes`, then `npm run eval:routes`. sideEffect (required for every skill) = true when the skill acts outside the conversation (deploy, push, publish, tracker, fleet or memory writes, settings, long loops); such a skill is offered as a menu and never auto-run. worker = true when a fleet or workflow worker may load the skill on its own (`ccc next` skill and skills, route-task.mjs, ccc-fleet-run args.skills): visible, no side effect, and its main path works in one thread without starting other agents; every other skill is never handed to a worker.",
